# --- Database (Neon Postgres recommended: https://neon.tech) ---
# The pooled connection string, used by the app at runtime.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require"
# Optional: a direct (non-pooled) connection string, used only for running
# migrations. On Neon, toggle "Pooled connection" off in Connection Details
# to get this one. If omitted, migrations fall back to DATABASE_URL, which
# works for a plain (non-Neon) Postgres but can fail against Neon's pooler.
DIRECT_URL=""
# Optional, and only needed to AUTHOR a migration locally. `prisma migrate dev`
# replays the existing migrations into a scratch database to work out what
# changed, and this is that scratch database — its contents are destroyed. Leave
# it unset in production, where migrations are only ever applied and nothing is
# diffed. Never point it at a database with anything in it.
SHADOW_DATABASE_URL=""

# --- Auth (Auth.js / NextAuth) ---
# Generate with: npx auth secret
AUTH_SECRET="replace-with-a-long-random-string"
NEXTAUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# --- Where this deployment lives ---
#
# The public address of the app, used to build absolute URLs that leave it: the
# hosted lead form a customer's ad points at, and the pages Stripe returns to
# after checkout. Wrong or unset in production and an ad can end up pointing at
# a URL that does not resolve, which is a live campaign spending money on a
# dead link.
#
# On Vercel this falls back to VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL, the project's
# production domain, which is injected automatically and cannot be mistyped —
# so leave it unset there unless the app is served from a custom domain that
# differs from it. Off Vercel it falls back to localhost, which is wrong for
# anything public. No trailing slash.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=""

# --- Meta (Facebook) Marketing API ---
# From your Meta App at https://developers.facebook.com/apps
META_APP_ID=""
META_APP_SECRET=""
# Optional. On Vercel this is derived automatically from the project's
# production domain, so leave it unset there. Set it only to override that
# (e.g. a custom domain that differs from the Vercel one). Whatever the app
# resolves it to must be registered verbatim under Valid OAuth Redirect URIs
# on the Meta App — see /aios/setup in the running app, which prints it.
META_REDIRECT_URI=""
# Optional, and for App Review only. Narrows the permissions the Facebook login
# dialog asks for to a comma-separated subset, so a screencast recorded for a
# submission shows exactly the permissions that submission covers — Meta
# rejects a video that asks for more than it claims to need. Clear it once the
# round is approved, or the features relying on the permissions left out will
# stop working for anyone who connects while it is set.
#   e.g. META_SCOPES="ads_management,ads_read,pages_show_list,business_management"
META_SCOPES=""
# Optional. Defaults to v21.0. Meta retires a Graph version roughly every two
# years and the calls in src/lib/meta/ are written against the default — so
# moving this forward is a deliberate upgrade to test, not a value to bump
# because a newer number exists.
META_GRAPH_API_VERSION=""

# --- TikTok Business API ---
# From your app at https://business-api.tiktok.com/portal/docs
#
# Leave these blank and TikTok simply isn't offered: the platform registry
# reports it as unconfigured, the campaign form doesn't show it, and nothing
# tries to make a call that cannot succeed. Fill them in and it switches on.
TIKTOK_APP_ID=""
TIKTOK_APP_SECRET=""
# Optional, and derived from the Vercel production domain when unset — same
# reasoning as META_REDIRECT_URI. Whatever it resolves to must be registered
# verbatim as an Advertiser Redirect URL on the TikTok app, with no trailing
# slash, or TikTok blocks the whole login.
TIKTOK_REDIRECT_URI=""
# Optional. Defaults to v1.3.
TIKTOK_API_VERSION=""

# --- TikTok posting (Login Kit) ---
#
# A SEPARATE registration from the advertising one above, and not
# interchangeable with it. TikTok has two APIs that share a name: the Business
# API (TIKTOK_APP_ID/SECRET) buys ad placements, and the Open API below posts
# videos to the customer's own profile. Different portal, different
# credentials, different consent screen, and an advertiser token is rejected by
# the posting endpoints.
#
# Leave these blank and "MAIRO posts to your TikTok" reports itself as
# unconfigured. Advertising is unaffected.
TIKTOK_CLIENT_KEY=""
TIKTOK_CLIENT_SECRET=""
# Optional, derived from the Vercel production domain when unset. Must be
# registered verbatim on the Login Kit app: <domain>/api/tiktok/creator/callback
TIKTOK_CREATOR_REDIRECT_URI=""
# Set to 1 only once TikTok has approved this app for direct posting.
#
# Until they have, TikTok forces everything an unaudited app posts to private,
# whatever the request asks for — so MAIRO puts videos in the customer's drafts
# and says so, rather than promising a public post and quietly delivering a
# private one. Turning this on before the approval lands would make the product
# lie about where a customer's video went.
TIKTOK_CONTENT_AUDITED=""

# --- AI agents (Claude) ---
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""
# Optional. Defaults to https://api.anthropic.com. Set it only to route through
# a proxy or gateway that speaks the same API.
ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=""

# Encrypts every advertising network access token before it is stored.
#
# These tokens are credentials for your clients' ad accounts — anyone holding
# one can create campaigns and spend that business's money. Without this key
# they sit in the database as plain text, so a leaked backup or a
# misconfigured replica hands them over intact.
#
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -base64 32
#
# Losing it means the stored connections cannot be read and every client has
# to reconnect, so keep a copy somewhere safe. Tokens written before it was
# set keep working and are encrypted the next time they are saved.
TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=""

# --- Owner recovery (leave unset normally) ---
# Set this temporarily to reopen /setup as a recovery page when an OWNER
# account exists but nobody can sign in as one. Visit /setup?token=<value>,
# reset the account, then DELETE this variable — while it is set, anyone
# holding the token can take over the owner account.
OWNER_SETUP_TOKEN=""

# --- Ad picture generation (Google Gemini image model) ---
# Claude reads pictures but cannot make them, so pictures come from Google.
# Free tier exists for testing; note that free tiers generally permit the
# provider to train on your data — use a paid key before real customer photos.
GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=""
# Optional override if Google renames the image model.
IMAGE_MODEL=""


# ── Payments (Stripe) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Subscribing and cancelling both happen on Stripe's hosted pages, so no card
# details ever reach this application.
#
# The secret key from dashboard.stripe.com/apikeys. Use the test key
# (sk_test_...) until you are ready to charge real cards.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=""

# From the webhook endpoint you create at dashboard.stripe.com/webhooks,
# pointed at https://your-domain/api/stripe/webhook. Without this the webhook
# refuses every delivery — it is what proves an event really came from Stripe
# and not from someone granting themselves a paid plan.
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""

# The price ids for each plan, created under Products in Stripe. Not secret.
# A plan with no price id set simply is not offered for sale.
#
# The prices in src/lib/plans.ts are only what the pricing page DISPLAYS. What
# a customer is charged is the Stripe Price behind these ids, so changing one
# without the other makes the page lie, and nothing fails when they disagree —
# the first anyone knows is a card statement. /aios/setup in the running app
# reads each price back out of Stripe and shows where the two differ.
#
# (`npm run plans:sync` is a different check: it compares the code against the
# PlanConfig table, which overrides it in the app. Neither one covers the
# other.)
STRIPE_PRICE_STARTER=""
STRIPE_PRICE_GROWTH=""
# The top business plan. This variable keeps the SCALE name whatever the plan
# is called on the website — the tier enum is what Stripe subscriptions are
# matched against, so renaming it would leave every existing subscriber
# matching no price id, which the webhook reads as having no plan at all.
# src/lib/plans.ts is the single place the plan is named and priced; this file
# deliberately does not repeat either, because a copy here goes stale.
STRIPE_PRICE_SCALE=""

# The freelancer plans, sold on /for-freelancers rather than the main pricing
# page. Both are optional in the same way as the others: leave one unset and
# that plan cannot be bought, which is the right behaviour while its price does
# not exist in Stripe yet, not an error.
STRIPE_PRICE_STUDIO=""
STRIPE_PRICE_AGENCY=""

# Set to 1 to actually enforce plan limits on organizations that have not paid.
#
# Left unset, everyone is treated as being on Starter and nothing is gated —
# which is how MAIRO launched and what the Meta App Review submission promises
# the reviewer. Turn this on only once App Review has completed.
BILLING_ENFORCED=""

# --- Google Tag Manager provisioning (optional) ---
#
# Lets MAIRO write conversion tags straight into a customer's Tag Manager and
# publish them, instead of handing them a file to import. Leave blank and the
# product says so and offers the download, which does the same job.
#
# Needs a Google Cloud project with the Tag Manager API enabled and an OAuth
# client of type "Web application". The scopes are sensitive, so Google has to
# verify the consent screen before anyone outside the project's test users can
# connect — until then, connecting works only for those accounts.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=""
# Optional, derived from the Vercel production domain when unset. Must be
# registered verbatim on the OAuth client: <domain>/api/gtm/callback
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=""

# --- Scheduled campaign starts ---
#
# Guards /api/cron/launch, which is what puts a campaign live at the time the
# customer booked. Vercel sends this automatically as a bearer token on the
# schedule in vercel.json; the route refuses every request without it, so
# leaving it blank means scheduled starts only happen when somebody opens the
# dashboard. Any long random string.
CRON_SECRET=""

# --- Text message updates (optional) ---
#
# Lets the assistant text a customer when their campaign goes live, when their
# advertising needs a look, or when MAIRO moves budget. Entirely optional: with
# these blank the product still offers the setting, but the server refuses the
# verification text and says why, rather than accepting a number and silently
# never using it.
#
# From a Twilio account: the Account SID and Auth Token are on the console
# dashboard, and the from-number is a number you have bought there, in E.164
# form (+15551234567). In production TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN is a Secret, the other
# two are Config.
#
# US and Canadian numbers need A2P 10DLC registration with Twilio before
# they will deliver to normal mobiles. Until that clears, sends are rejected
# by the carrier and the reason comes back in the server log.
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=""
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=""
TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER=""
